Task: Implement smart backup logic in install_coverage_addon

Summary:
- Modified install_coverage_addon in src/gd_tools/init.py to compare existing
  coverage addon files against bundled versions before overwriting.
- If content differs (user modification detected), the existing file is backed
  up to addons/gd-tools-coverage/.backups/<filename>.bak before overwrite.
- A yellow warning is printed via console.print naming the file and backup path.
- The .backups/ directory is auto-created if it does not exist.
- Unchanged files are overwritten silently (no backup, no warning).
- First-time install behavior is unchanged (no existing files to compare).

Files modified:
- src/gd_tools/init.py: Updated install_coverage_addon with backup logic
- tests/unit/test_init.py: Added 6 new tests + updated 1 existing test

Why: Re-running gd-tools init previously destroyed user customizations to
coverage addon files with no backup or warning. This provides a recovery path.
